# The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt (next-gen, 4.x)
# summary: Skips the launcher, DLSS through OptiScaler (pick XeSS in the game), the online-check hitch every 100 ms gone
# Skip CDPR's REDprelauncher; the game is DirectX 12 only and its graphics settings are in dx12user.settings, which
# bench/games/witcher3.sh sets per run.
EXTRA_ARGS=--launcher-skip
# DLSS: the game's own path (Streamline 2.14.1) never starts NVIDIA's NGX here (docs/FINDINGS.md), so OptiScaler
# (bin/x64_dx12/dxgi.dll; MANIFEST-optiscaler.txt there) takes the game's XeSS calls and runs DLSS through NGX
# itself; the game's FSR stays FSR. At 4K: FSR Quality 59 fps (settings candidate D), XeSS Performance = DLSS
# Performance 55 (candidate E; CNN model), DLSS Quality 37-39, XeSS Native AA = DLAA 22: DLSS is costly on GB10.
# NGX needs NVIDIA's API exposed to the game.
PROTON_ENABLE_NVAPI=1
# The main loop asks wininet "am I online?" ~10 times a second; Wine answers each with a full network-interface scan
# (~35 ms under FEX), a hitch every ~100 ms. The shim caches the answer (system/shim.sh install 292030).
SHIM=powrprof@bin/x64_dx12
WINEDLLOVERRIDES=powrprof=n,b;dxgi=n,b
